IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il33-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il33-readings`
IMPORT `nii-il33-fixtures`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-a1-ages`
IMPORT `nii-s2a-residence`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests: s 2A (who is not an Israeli resident) and the words "sits in Israel" of s 65(a). Row IL-33.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the Hebrew (lines 241-257, 803) before the run.
-- The Law gives no positive test of residence: a person is a resident here if the case says he lives in
-- Israel and s 2A does not exclude the stay (fork R1).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — s 2A`

§§ `The stays that exclude without condition (b)(1), (2), (3), (3A), (5)`

-- (b)(1) present unlawfully; (b)(2) a permit under the Entry Order; (b)(3) a visitor B/1 to B/4; (b)(3A)
-- regulation 5A; (b)(5) A/3 and a relative holding A/4. Each lives in Israel; none is a resident.
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` `unlawful presence within section 13 of the Entry to Israel Law`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` `a permit under the Entry to Israel Order (exemption of residents of Judea and Samaria, the Gaza Strip and northern Sinai, central Sinai, the Sharm el-Sheikh area and the Golan Heights), 5728-1968`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` `a visitor's visa and licence of type B/1, B/2, B/3 or B/4, under regulation 5 of the Entry Regulations`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` `a visa and licence under regulation 5A of the Entry Regulations`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` `a temporary-residence visa and licence of type A/3 (regulation 6(c)), or of type A/4 as a relative of the holder of A/3 (regulation 6(d)), of the Entry Regulations`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- No permission section 2A names (a citizen, an oleh): a resident if he lives in Israel.
#ASSERT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` `no permission that section 2A names`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- A person who does not live in Israel is not one, whatever his papers say (fork R1).
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a person` "Abroad" `born` (YMD 1990 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` `a person living abroad` `and` `the work of an employee in Israel`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)

§§ `An A/1 visa, (b)(4): the determining year and the two limbs`

-- Granted on 1 September 2025. The determining year begins 183 days earlier, on 2 March 2025: counting forward
-- from 2 March, 2 April is 31 days on, 2 May 61, 2 June 92, 2 July 122, 2 August 153 and 2 September 184, so
-- 1 September is 183 days after 2 March. The year is twelve consecutive months from that day: 2 March 2025 to
-- 1 March 2026 inclusive.
#ASSERT `s 2A — the first day of the determining year of a visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 2
#ASSERT `s 2A — the day` (YMD 2025 3 2) `falls in the determining year of a visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — the day` (YMD 2025 3 1) `falls in the determining year of a visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1)
#ASSERT `s 2A — the day` (YMD 2026 3 1) `falls in the determining year of a visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — the day` (YMD 2026 3 2) `falls in the determining year of a visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1)
-- Fewer than 183 days (100): (a) excludes the whole determining year; (b) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 100 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 100 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 100 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 100 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2025 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 100 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2025 3 2)
-- More than 183 days (200): (b) excludes the period before the visa day; the year after it is not excluded.
#ASSERT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 200 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 200 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2025 8 31)
#ASSERT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 200 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2025 9 1)
-- (d): the Institute regards the holder as a resident from the visa day. From that day on the (a) exclusion
-- is lifted; before it (a) and (b) stand.
#ASSERT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 100 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` TRUE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 100 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` TRUE)) `on` (YMD 2025 9 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 100 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` TRUE)) `on` (YMD 2025 8 31)

§§ `Exactly 183 days (fork R4)`

-- The limbs say fewer than 183 and more than 183. At exactly 183 days:
--   "counted with fewer": (a) applies, so the determining year is excluded, and (b) does not;
--   "counted with more": (b) applies, so the period before the visa day is excluded, and (a) does not;
--   "neither": nothing is excluded.
-- Asked on 15 January 2026 (in the year, after the visa day): fewer -> excluded; more -> not; neither -> not.
-- They differ, so the default declines.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 183 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 183 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading 183 as` `183 days is counted with fewer than 183 days`
#ASSERT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 183 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading 183 as` `183 days is counted with more than 183 days`
#ASSERT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 183 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading 183 as` `183 days falls under neither limb, as the words read`
-- Asked on 1 January 2027 (after the year and the visa day): all three readings agree, so the default answers.
#ASSERT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 183 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2027 1 1)
-- Asked on 1 June 2025 (before the visa day, in the year): fewer -> excluded by (a); more -> excluded by (b);
-- neither -> not excluded. They differ: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 183 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2025 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 183 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2025 6 1) `, reading 183 as` `183 days is counted with more than 183 days`
#ASSERT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`an A/1 visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 183 `days, section 2A(d) decision:` FALSE)) `on` (YMD 2025 6 1) `, reading 183 as` `183 days falls under neither limb, as the words read`

§§ `Another visa and licence, (c)`

-- The same two limbs, without (d). Granted 1 September 2025; 100 days: the year is excluded.
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`another visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 100 `days`)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`another visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 200 `days`)) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` (`a man living in Israel under` (`another visa granted on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `with` 200 `days`)) `on` (YMD 2025 8 31)

§ `Tests — s 65(a) "מבוטח" (2): sits in Israel (fork R3)`

-- A visitor (B/2) who in fact lives in Israel: s 2A excludes him, so on the reading that "sits in" is
-- "resident" he does not sit in Israel; on the reading that it is a matter of fact he does; by default the
-- two differ and the question is declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 65(a) — sits in Israel:` (`a man living in Israel under` `a visitor's visa and licence of type B/1, B/2, B/3 or B/4, under regulation 5 of the Entry Regulations`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 65(a) — sits in Israel:` (`a man living in Israel under` `a visitor's visa and licence of type B/1, B/2, B/3 or B/4, under regulation 5 of the Entry Regulations`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading the words as` `sits in Israel is residence within section 2A` `and 183 days as` `exactly 183 days is declined where the readings differ`
#ASSERT `s 65(a) — sits in Israel:` (`a man living in Israel under` `a visitor's visa and licence of type B/1, B/2, B/3 or B/4, under regulation 5 of the Entry Regulations`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading the words as` `sits in Israel is a matter of fact, whatever section 2A says` `and 183 days as` `exactly 183 days is declined where the readings differ`
-- A person section 2A does not touch who lives in Israel: all readings agree.
#ASSERT `s 65(a) — sits in Israel:` (`a man living in Israel under` `no permission that section 2A names`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- A person who does not live in Israel: all readings agree (not).
#ASSERT NOT `s 65(a) — sits in Israel:` (`a person` "Abroad" `born` (YMD 1990 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` `a person living abroad` `and` `the work of an employee in Israel`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15)

§ `Tests — the residence part of limb (2) as a whole`

-- A resident who is absent beyond a reasonable temporary absence, in the Institute's opinion: not.
#ASSERT `s 65(a) — lives in Israel as limb (2) requires:` (`a man living in Israel under` `no permission that section 2A names`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading the words as` `sits in Israel is residence within section 2A` `and 183 days as` `exactly 183 days is declined where the readings differ`
#ASSERT NOT `s 65(a) — lives in Israel as limb (2) requires:` (`a person` "Away" `born` (YMD 1990 1 1) `who is` `male` `with` (`The residence facts of a person` WITH `lives in Israel` IS TRUE, `permission to stay` IS `no permission that section 2A names`, `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence` IS TRUE, `the day the person first became an Israeli resident` IS NOTHING, `a temporary resident` IS FALSE) `and` `the work of an employee in Israel`) `on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading the words as` `sits in Israel is residence within section 2A` `and 183 days as` `exactly 183 days is declined where the readings differ`
